---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "ItemList",
  "name": "Operator Stack",
  "description": "Tools Pravine Mani uses daily. AI workflows. SEO. Marketing automation consulting. Real costs. What gets deliberately avoided.",
  "url": "https://pravinemani.com/stack/"
};
---

<Base title="Operator Stack · Tools I Build With Daily · Pravine Mani" description="Opinionated operator stack. Claude Code. Vercel. Next.js. Supabase. MCP. Daily tools. Real costs. What I deliberately avoid: n8n, Make, Zapier." jsonLd={jsonLd}>


<section class="page-hero">
  <div class="breadcrumb"><span class="gr">$</span> cat ~/.stack <span class="you">→ the operator stack</span></div>
  <h1>The operator stack.<br><span class="accent">Every tool. Why. What it costs.</span></h1>
  <p class="lead">The tools I run on every engagement, ranked by frequency. Costs are honest and personal. The full monthly burn is at the bottom. What I deliberately don't use is at the bottom too, because the absence is the point.</p>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="principle-block">
    <div class="lab">THE RULE</div>
    <p>Code in the repo, secrets in env vars, logs in Vercel, schedule in cron. Every workflow runs on infrastructure the client already owns. The stack disappears with the engagement — nothing in my account, nothing on a platform that can sunset.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="legend">
    <span><span class="green">●</span> DAILY · used on every project</span>
    <span>○ OCCASIONAL · case-by-case</span>
    <span class="avoid-tag">AVOIDED · code-first replaces this</span>
  </div>

  <div class="stack-cat">
    <div class="sc-head">
      <div class="name"><span class="n">01 ·</span> CODE + SHIP</div>
      <div class="cost">USAGE-BASED</div>
    </div>
    <div class="tool-rows">
      <div class="tool daily">
        <div class="nm daily">Claude Code</div>
        <div class="why">The development surface. Sub-agents, MCP, hooks, headless mode. Replaces an IDE, a pair-programmer, and a research assistant.</div>
        <div class="price">PAID</div>
        <div class="tag">DAILY</div>
      </div>
      <div class="tool daily">
        <div class="nm daily">Vercel</div>
        <div class="why">Hosting, serverless, cron, edge config, KV. Every client deploy ships through Vercel Pro. Build logs are the deliverable receipt.</div>
        <div class="price">PAID</div>
        <div class="tag">DAILY</div>
      </div>
      <div class="tool daily">
        <div class="nm daily">TypeScript</div>
        <div class="why">Default for anything past a one-file script. Strict mode. Type-check passes before any commit lands.</div>
        <div class="price">FREE</div>
        <div class="tag">DAILY</div>
      </div>
      <div class="tool daily">
        <div class="nm daily">GitHub</div>
        <div class="why">Repo, PR review, Actions for CI, Issues for client-facing scope. Every engagement gets its own private repo handed off at close.</div>
        <div class="price">FREE / PAID</div>
        <div class="tag">DAILY</div>
      </div>
      <div class="tool">
        <div class="nm">Cursor</div>
        <div class="why">Secondary editor when a tight inline-completion loop beats Claude Code's chat surface. Same Anthropic models underneath.</div>
        <div class="price">PAID</div>
        <div class="tag">OCCASIONAL</div>
      </div>
      <div class="tool">
        <div class="nm">v0</div>
        <div class="why">First-pass UI scaffolds. Generated React + Tailwind, ported to production-grade components after.</div>
        <div class="price">USAGE-BASED</div>
        <div class="tag">OCCASIONAL</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="stack-cat">
    <div class="sc-head">
      <div class="name"><span class="n">02 ·</span> AI + AGENTS</div>
      <div class="cost">USAGE-BASED</div>
    </div>
    <div class="tool-rows">
      <div class="tool daily">
        <div class="nm daily">Anthropic API</div>
        <div class="why">Claude 4.7 Opus for code and reasoning, Sonnet 4.6 for high-volume work. Prompt caching cuts ~70% of token cost on stable system prompts.</div>
        <div class="price">USAGE-BASED</div>
        <div class="tag">DAILY</div>
      </div>
      <div class="tool daily">
        <div class="nm daily">MCP</div>
        <div class="why">Model Context Protocol. Filesystem, GitHub, Playwright, Obsidian, plus custom servers shipped per client engagement.</div>
        <div class="price">FREE PROTOCOL</div>
        <div class="tag">DAILY</div>
      </div>
      <div class="tool">
        <div class="nm">OpenAI / GPT-5</div>
        <div class="why">Comparison runs and specific tasks where GPT pulls ahead. Not primary.</div>
        <div class="price">USAGE-BASED</div>
        <div class="tag">OCCASIONAL</div>
      </div>
      <div class="tool">
        <div class="nm">Gemini 3 / NotebookLM</div>
        <div class="why">Research synthesis. 1M-token context window. Audio overviews are the 10x feature.</div>
        <div class="price">FREE / PAID</div>
        <div class="tag">OCCASIONAL</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="stack-cat">
    <div class="sc-head">
      <div class="name"><span class="n">03 ·</span> DATA + INFRA</div>
      <div class="cost">USAGE-BASED</div>
    </div>
    <div class="tool-rows">
      <div class="tool daily">
        <div class="nm daily">Supabase</div>
        <div class="why">Postgres + auth + RLS. Default database on every client build. Row-Level Security replaces about 80% of the auth code most apps end up writing by hand.</div>
        <div class="price">FREE / PAID</div>
        <div class="tag">DAILY</div>
      </div>
      <div class="tool daily">
        <div class="nm daily">Vercel KV</div>
        <div class="why">Redis-compatible key-value store on Vercel. Idempotency keys, session state, cron memory, prompt cache.</div>
        <div class="price">USAGE-BASED</div>
        <div class="tag">DAILY</div>
      </div>
      <div class="tool daily">
        <div class="nm daily">Vercel Cron</div>
        <div class="why">Scheduled serverless functions. Code in the repo, versioned, debuggable in build logs. The replacement for n8n / Make for every scheduled workflow.</div>
        <div class="price">INCLUDED</div>
        <div class="tag">DAILY</div>
      </div>
      <div class="tool daily">
        <div class="nm daily">Resend</div>
        <div class="why">Transactional email. Clean SDK, fast DKIM setup, sane deliverability. Default mail provider on every engagement.</div>
        <div class="price">FREE / PAID</div>
        <div class="tag">DAILY</div>
      </div>
      <div class="tool daily">
        <div class="nm daily">Stripe</div>
        <div class="why">Checkout + Customer Portal + webhooks. The lookup-and-paste API. Idempotency-key handling on the webhook side is the line most builds forget.</div>
        <div class="price">USAGE-BASED</div>
        <div class="tag">DAILY</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="stack-cat">
    <div class="sc-head">
      <div class="name"><span class="n">04 ·</span> CONTENT + GROWTH</div>
      <div class="cost">USAGE-BASED</div>
    </div>
    <div class="tool-rows">
      <div class="tool daily">
        <div class="nm daily">Beehiiv</div>
        <div class="why">Newsletter. 0% on paid subs. Built-in ads marketplace. Boost Network for cross-promo growth.</div>
        <div class="price">FREE / PAID</div>
        <div class="tag">DAILY</div>
      </div>
      <div class="tool daily">
        <div class="nm daily">Plausible</div>
        <div class="why">Privacy-friendly analytics. No cookie banner. EU-friendly. Replaced GA4 across every client engagement.</div>
        <div class="price">PAID</div>
        <div class="tag">DAILY</div>
      </div>
      <div class="tool">
        <div class="nm">Whop</div>
        <div class="why">Community + checkout. 3% platform + Stripe. The marketplace discoverability is the actual win.</div>
        <div class="price">USAGE-BASED</div>
        <div class="tag">OCCASIONAL</div>
      </div>
      <div class="tool">
        <div class="nm">Typefully</div>
        <div class="why">X scheduling. Clean editor. Thread split. Cross-posts to LinkedIn, Threads, Bluesky.</div>
        <div class="price">PAID</div>
        <div class="tag">OCCASIONAL</div>
      </div>
      <div class="tool">
        <div class="nm">AuthoredUp</div>
        <div class="why">LinkedIn editor + analytics. Best value at launch tier. Skip Taplio until you're scaling LI seriously.</div>
        <div class="price">PAID</div>
        <div class="tag">OCCASIONAL</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="stack-cat avoid">
    <div class="sc-head">
      <div class="name"><span class="n">05 ·</span> DELIBERATELY NOT USING</div>
      <div class="cost">REPLACED BY CODE-FIRST</div>
    </div>
    <div class="tool-rows">
      <div class="tool">
        <div class="nm">n8n</div>
        <div class="why">Visual workflow tool. Replaced with Vercel cron + serverless functions on the client's own infrastructure. No platform fee. Versioned in git. Debuggable when something breaks at 3am.</div>
        <div class="price">FREE / PAID</div>
        <div class="tag">AVOIDED</div>
      </div>
      <div class="tool">
        <div class="nm">Make.com</div>
        <div class="why">Same as n8n. Fine for non-technical users. Wrong fit for an operator who can write a serverless function in 20 minutes.</div>
        <div class="price">PAID</div>
        <div class="tag">AVOIDED</div>
      </div>
      <div class="tool">
        <div class="nm">Zapier</div>
        <div class="why">Even more expensive per-action than the above. The cost-per-workflow at scale doesn't make sense once you can code.</div>
        <div class="price">PAID</div>
        <div class="tag">AVOIDED</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


</Base>
<style is:global>
.stack-cat { background: var(--bg-card); border: 1px solid var(--border); margin-bottom: 20px; position: relative; }
.stack-cat::before { content: ''; position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; right: 0; height: 2px; background: var(--card-accent, var(--green)); opacity: 0.8; }
.sc-head { padding: 18px 26px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); background: var(--bg-tertiary); display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; }
.sc-head .name { font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.16em; color: var(--green); text-transform: uppercase; }
.sc-head .name .n { color: var(--text-dim); }
.sc-head .cost { font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: 0.1em; color: var(--text-dim); text-transform: uppercase; }
.sc-head .cost .v { color: var(--text-primary); }
.tool-rows { padding: 0; }
.tool { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 200px 1fr auto auto; gap: 18px; align-items: center; padding: 14px 26px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
.tool:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
.tool .nm { font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-primary); }
.tool .nm.daily::after { content: ' ●'; color: var(--green); font-size: 12px; }
.tool .why { font-family: 'IBM Plex Sans', sans-serif; font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.5; }
.tool .price { font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 11px; color: var(--text-dim); letter-spacing: 0.06em; text-align: right; }
.tool .tag { font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 9px; letter-spacing: 0.12em; text-transform: uppercase; padding: 3px 7px; border: 1px solid currentColor; color: var(--text-dim); }
.tool.daily .tag { color: var(--green); }
.tool.optional .tag { color: var(--text-dim); }
.stack-cat:nth-of-type(1) { --card-accent: var(--green); }
.stack-cat:nth-of-type(2) { --card-accent: var(--red); }
.stack-cat:nth-of-type(3) { --card-accent: #a855f7; }
.stack-cat:nth-of-type(4) { --card-accent: var(--blue); }
.stack-cat:nth-of-type(5) { --card-accent: #1e40af; }
.stack-cat.avoid { border-color: rgba(255, 68, 68, 0.2); }
.stack-cat.avoid::before { background: var(--red); }
.stack-cat.avoid .sc-head .name { color: var(--red); }
.legend { font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.08em; color: var(--text-dim); text-transform: uppercase; padding: 14px 22px; background: var(--bg-card); border: 1px solid var(--border); margin-bottom: 24px; display: flex; gap: 24px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
.legend .green { color: var(--green); }
@media (max-width: 720px) { .tool { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 6px; padding: 14px 20px; } .tool .price, .tool .tag { text-align: left; } }
</style>
